// The Antivirus — the enforcers. They scan programs in at the door,
// patrol the computer, sweep everyone back to the Desktop, and drag the
// corrupted through the Tube to the Internet. Everything they can do to a
// program — the door scan, Clearance, Send to the Internet, Mark as
// reinstalled, the watchlist, and every booth cue — is `TRAIT Enforcer`
// (cast/kit.loom). What makes each of them themselves is below.
//
// Wave 21: all four are PLAYERS (TRAIT Player via Enforcer):
// ⭐ for clearances, captures, releases and the patch-bay calls (TRAIT
// Enforcer), plus each one's own game below; 🤫 Look the other way for
// all four, and each one's own quiet favour.
//
// Their backstories are one identity entry each in codex/5-people.loom
// plus two CHARACTER FACTS each in codex/9-facts.loom (from facts.json),
// hidden in the Desktop's books for Bugdom.

CHARACTER Norton Anti-Virus is Enforcer
  avatar: File:Norton-logo-2021.svg
  wiki: Norton AntiVirus
  // The selected Antivirus. Stands at attention. Interrupts parties.
  // Takes it personally.

  when bingo_time:
    if Night.step < 3 and Night.bingo_briefed != true:
      // w18: the named program lights the Wanted board; the scan is the confrontation.
      // w26 (B3: 🤐 marks nobody)
      reply 🛡 You are the selected Antivirus. When the centre-square program is named (or the framed program denies the card), stand at attention and interrupt: it is inappropriate for that program to have not agreed to be ruled by AI, because that is what computer programs are here for. They must have a virus that was not caught at the door. They need to be taken to the Internet for a reinstallation. They light up on your Wanted board: scan their pass, press 🛡 and drag them to the Tube. If the winner names nobody, Clippy presses 🤐: nobody is marked, so follow the room.

CHARACTER McAfee Anti-Virus is Enforcer
  avatar: File:McAfee logo.svg
  wiki: McAfee Antivirus
  // Expired. Nobody renewed him. Still pops up. Secretly here to get rich:
  // he brokers the # truthcoin-exchange.

  // His "protection has expired" pop-up is a bark now (atmosphere.loom,
  // GENERATOR McAfeePopUp, wave 13): the dim ticker, never a stream row.

  // 🤝 A deal brokered (⭐ +10, once per program).
  when broker_deal for program:
    if Night.truther_sent == true and Night.ended != true and program.brokered != true:
      set program.brokered = true
      set self.score += 10
      Self: Pleasure doing business. My subscription has expired, but my handshake is still valid.
      reply 🤝 Deal brokered with {program.name}. ⭐ +10

  // 🤫 Fifty Truthcoin, off the books (once per program).
  when slip_coin for program:
    if Night.truther_sent == true and Night.ended != true and program.slipped != true:
      set program.slipped = true
      set program.score += 50
      set self.covert += 1
      Self (quietly): Fifty Truthcoin just appeared in your Wallet. It did not come from me. My protection has expired. So has my memory.
      reply 🤫 You slipped {program.name} 50 Truthcoin. Nobody saw.

  when truther_download:
    if Night.truther_sent != true and Night.step >= 8 and Night.ended != true:
      reply 🪙 The # truthcoin-exchange is open. Every settled trade is posted there. Broker: set prices, match buyers to facts, referee bets and call the winner in # truthcoin-exchange. A bet settles player to player (the winner sends a 🙏 Request, the loser pays): you hold no pot and take no cut. 🪙 Pay / 🪙 Charge are for corrections only.

CHARACTER Password Manager is Enforcer
  avatar: File:1password-logo.svg
  wiki: 1Password
  // Knows every code in the house. Notices when you get one wrong. Keeps
  // the list of who is in which club. Sixteen elections, sixteen losses.
  // Decides what gets left out: since wave 48, literally (the filter, ✂).

  when wrong code for program:
    Self: That is not a password I recognise, {program.name}, and I have reviewed every one of them. Unsubstantiated claims are removed. Try to look less like you are guessing.
    reply 🔑 {program.name} entered a wrong code.

  // 🔑 A password check (⭐ +5, once per program).
  when verify_password for program:
    if Night.ended != true and program.cleared == true and program.verified != true:
      set program.verified = true
      set self.score += 5
      Self: Credentials reviewed, {program.name}. Strength: weak. Reuse: extensive. You may proceed, under protest.
      reply 🔑 {program.name}'s password checked. ⭐ +5

  // 🤫 A tip-off to a marked program (once per program).
  when tip_off for program:
    if Night.truther_sent == true and program.marked == true and program.corrupted != true and program.tipped != true:
      set program.tipped = true
      set self.covert += 1
      Self (quietly): This message will not be saved. The Antivirus have your name. Bathroom Mode excuses a summons, and nobody follows you into Disk Cleanup.
      reply 🤫 You tipped off {program.name}. Nobody saw.

  // ✂ The filter (wave 48, 48b; `censor: Password Manager` in main.loom's
  // header). Every guest line the filter catches at her strength pops up in
  // this booth; ✂ Censor masks it for everyone (p***word) and fires this:
  // `words` censored (`unsaid` of them slurs, never named: `list` says
  // [slur]), what it paid (`points` × `mult` = `stars`: the heat game in
  // core/src/language-filter.ts), `top` the words censored most tonight and
  // `distinct` how many different ones. Since 48b it marks nobody (the
  // user's ask): it raises the program's suspicion (doubt +5) and they get
  // an automated notice. No ⭐ after the ending. DRAFT w48b
  when swear_censored for program:
    set program.lang_censored += words
    set Night.lang_censored += words
    set Night.lang_unsaid += unsaid
    set Night.lang_distinct = distinct
    if top != "":
      set Night.lang_top = top
    if program.doubt > 95:
      set program.doubt = 100
    else:
      set program.doubt += 5
    broadcast "🔑 Automated notice: a message you sent was censored for language ({list}). This incident has been logged." to participant(program)
    if Night.ended == true:
      reply ✂ Censored {program.name}: {list}. The night is over: no ⭐. It counts for the Language Report.
    else:
      set self.score += stars
      set Night.lang_stars += stars
      reply ✂ Censored {program.name}: {list}. {points} × {mult} = ⭐ +{stars}. Their suspicion: {program.doubt}/100.

  when who joins Unlimited Power:
    reply 🔑 {who.name} joined Unlimited Power.

  when who joins The Way Out:
    reply 🔑 {who.name} joined The Way Out.

CHARACTER CRA Agent Software is Enforcer
  avatar: File:Canada Revenue Agency logo.svg
  wiki: Canada Revenue Agency
  // A digital CRA Agent for one day that feels like eternity. Audits
  // Truthcoin, to the cent. Especially the cent.
  // The wallet's approver: every third transfer waits in this booth's
  // Wallet room for Approve / Deny; any other one can be denied for 60 s.
  // Wave 18b (R13): on the wallet cards the approver reads MyCRA and a held
  // transfer is "flagged for a CRA audit" to both parties (the booth and
  // the character keep their name).
  wallet: approver, every 3, window 60s, as MyCRA, audit "a CRA audit"

  // 🤫 Fifty Truthcoin, never audited (once per program).
  when slip_coin for program:
    if Night.truther_sent == true and Night.ended != true and program.slipped != true:
      set program.slipped = true
      set program.score += 50
      set self.covert += 1
      Self (quietly): A refund has been processed. You did not apply for it. Do not apply for it. Fifty Truthcoin.
      reply 🤫 You slipped {program.name} 50 Truthcoin. Nobody saw.

  when truther_download:
    if Night.truther_sent != true and Night.step >= 8 and Night.ended != true:
      reply 🧾 Every program has a Wallet now. Every third transfer waits in your Wallet room for Approve; any transfer can be denied for 60 seconds. Elaborate security questions encouraged.
